// UNWRAP OF A POINTER IS READ TWO WAYS, BOTH KEPT: the alias pass walks a function as main does, an unwrap no step and the place under it its root
// whole, and when that walk met an unwrap of a pointer it walks the function again with every unwrap a step to its operand (the longer path, which
// re-roots through the pointer), one report per site; escape roots a view through a local's or a field's unwrap too, and an unwrap whose value is
// itself a wrapped pointer steps as well. DEF-738'S PRICES (LOW, numbered at l.23500 item 5): the longer path roots a view through a wrapped
// local's own unwrap at that local, so a later reassignment of the local is refused. Every case runs 67 on main on every road 0-8 at -O0 and -O2
// and under the detector. Off parity where the local isn't this frame's `@` (the pointer twins run 67 here:
// tests/backend/programs/unwrap_reading_wayout_ok.npk, with the ways out); at parity where it is (the by-name twins, last here, are refused on
// main). Main already reads a wrapped PARAMETER this way (`ap3u_oqpp_ok`, R4-10's); this row extends it to locals.
mod:unwrap_reading_def738_prices;
